A||||9||The Fieromaster||Ran Into Ed Parks Today.... In Ohio!?!?!||||10||
Z||000000||The Fieromaster||10-10-2001||11:10 PM||||I was drivin to my buddies house in Mentor on the lake Ohio, from my house in Mayfield... When outta nowhere a van pulls in after us!  Im like wonder who this dood is and what he is doing here!?!?  So he comes up and asks us where a certain road is.  He said he followed me cause i have a Fiero and he is pickin up a caddy 4.9L from this guy who doenst want to buy it from him any more!  Im like its not me.  If you wanna sell it i may buy it.... But he tells me its already sold!  So i start gabbin Fiero's with him and my buddy is like... Dood he is a Fiero guy from Fiero Factory... Im like you are man (my buddy points out the pbvious i missed on his shirt) then i notice his name tag... "HOLY SHEEET" I think... Its Ed Parks!!  I couldnt believe it... Of ALL places he is by my BUDDIES house and I didnt even know there were that many fans out here!  Im like WOO HOO.  For any of you wonderin ED is COOL AS HELL!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> The guy is polite and a totaly great guy!!  I woulnt think for a second to deny him any business from me!  Well thats my day... Crazy and really cool!!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">       <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">    <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">               <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B>||||reg||10
Z||000001||mrtgman||10-10-2001||11:27 PM||||who is ed parks?||||reg||1
Z||000002||The Fieromaster||10-10-2001||11:57 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrtgman:<BR><B>who is ed parks?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Seriously?  Your kiddin?  He has the "Fiero Factory" the largesy "Fiero Junkyard" you name it he has it!  He also does swaps, and Fiero specific repairs there too! Here is his web site addy thanks to MooCow!! <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red">"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">     <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif"">                <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AIM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT></B><p>[This message has been edited by The Fieromaster (edited 10-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rick 88||10-11-2001||12:02 AM||||Ed Parks has devoted his life to the preservation of Fieros. Check out his business the Fiero Factory located in Alabama. Check out his web site for tips. <A HREF="http://www.welcome.to/thefierofactory" TARGET=_blank>www.welcome.to/thefierofactory</A>  Ed posts on the Fiero Digest. I have personally met Ed and can say that he and his wife are two of the nicest people I have met.<P>Rick 88||||reg||1
Z||000004||The Fieromaster||10-11-2001||12:05 AM||||AMEN Rick!||||reg||1
Z||000005||MooCow||10-11-2001||12:20 AM||||Yes I have met Ed Parks and Rossie three times now and everytime is better and better.  The Fiero Factory is an awsome place and his workers are just as nice and do very good work.  I had Ed build me a 3.4 with a 4:10 tranny and its an awsome car.  Can't wait to meet him again.  If you ever need any parts or any questions answered just call him or email him.  He knows it all.<BR>I have tried to get him onto the forum but he doesnt like computers all that much and mainly only uses his computer for email.  He told me that is any one has a question to just call him or email him.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_7.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||10
Z||000006||tgowens||10-11-2001||01:53 AM||||Ed would be a lot better friend of mine if he would send one of these out here (check out the 4.9's in the crates)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-578f.jpg"> <BR>.....George and I stopped in there a couple of weeks ago on my way back to KY to drop off one of my Fieros.....<BR>Here is Jeremy working on one of the 4.9's<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-577f.jpg"> <P>Now, here's a rare shot......George Miller of Fiero Shop in Richmond, CA with Ed Parks of Fiero Factory in Toney, AL together (that's the famous e-mail machine behind Ed!!)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Mvc-588f.jpg"> <P>Ed has had the Fiero Factory for the past 9 years and do believe Ed, Rosie, Jeremy, Rick and Dave to be some of the finest people I have met -- always there to help and will answer any Fiero question you may have......<P>(I guess that Rosie was runnin' the shop while he was up in the Buckeye state, huh? -- Good job Rosie!!)||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alex4mula||10-11-2001||08:33 AM||||If you don't know Ed Parks then you haven't been in the Fiero community long enough. Sooner or later you'll get to them. Same applies to Rodney, Archie, etc. etc...||||reg||1
Z||000008||PAUL88GT||10-11-2001||11:17 AM||||Just plan on attending the next swap meet at the Fiero Factory during the last weekend of April 2002. You can find some great deals on parts. Also, a good chance to view Ed's Fiero-only operation. Ed and Rosie are good people, but they are also running a business. They keep a lot of Fieros from ending up at the crusher. Hope to see ya'll at the next swap meet.<BR>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||10-11-2001||11:36 AM||||Yeah, Ed and Rosy are great people. I met them like three years ago, at the swap meet. Ed will go out of his way to help. <BR>Probably not a more knowledgeable Fiero fiend, anywhere. Or at least in <I>my</I> part of the world.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
